#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid "More &kgeography; features"
msgstr "Mais funcionalidades de &kgeography; "

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another feature of &kgeography; is the possibility of zoom on a map. "
"<screenshot> <screeninfo>Zoom</screeninfo> <mediaobject> <imageobject> "
"<imagedata fileref=\"zoom.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> "
"<phrase>Zoom</phrase> </textobject> </mediaobject> </screenshot> "
"While in zoom mode, you can press &RMB; to go back to the original map size "
"(the <guimenuitem>Original Size</guimenuitem> action has the same effect). Use "
"the scroll bars to move around the zoomed map or use the <guimenuitem>"
"Move</guimenuitem> action that will allow you to drag the map using &LMB;."
msgstr ""
"Outra funcionalidade de &kgeography; é a de ampliar un mapa. "
"<screenshot><screeninfo>Ampliacion</screeninfo><mediaobject><imageobject> "
"<imagedata fileref=\"zoom.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject><textobject> "
"<phrase>Ampliación</phrase></textobject></mediaobject></screenshot> "
"Mentres estexa no modo ampliación, poderá premer o &RMB; para voltar ao tamaño "
"orixinal do mapa (a acción <guimenuitem>Tamaño Orixinal</guimenuitem> fai o mesmo). "
"Use as barras de desprazamento arredor do mapa ampliado ou use a acción "
"<guimenuitem>Mover</guimenuitem> que lle permite arrastar e soltar o mapa co &LMB;."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to make maps"
msgstr "Como facer mapas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A map in &kgeography; is made by two files, one is the image of the map and the "
"other one is its description."
msgstr ""
"Un mapa de &kgeography; está composto de dous ficheiros, un é a imaxe do mapa e o outro é "
"a súa descripción."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid "Helper tool"
msgstr "Ferramenta auxiliar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:319
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can find <ulink url=\"http://kgeography.berlios.de/gen_map.pl\">here</ulink> "
"a tool (made by Yann Verley) which helped him with the map of France. To find "
"out its usage, simply execute it and read the help message. It basically "
"creates the <literal role=\"extension\">.kgm</literal> "
"file from a plain text file and creates a file with the colors it has assigned "
"to each division, so you can fill the map according to them."
msgstr ""
"Poderá achar <ulink url=\"http://kgeography.berlios.de/gen_map.pl\">aquí</ulink> unha "
"ferramenta (feita por Yann Verley) que o axudou co mapa da franza. Para aprender como "
"se usa, simplesmente execute-o e lea a mensaxe de axuda. En esencia cria o ficheiro "
"<literal role=\"extension\">.kgm</literal> e cria un ficheiro coas cores que asinase a "
"cada división, paa que poda preenche o mapa de acordo como el."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid "Description file"
msgstr "Ficheiro de descrición"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The description file is needed and its file extension is <literal "
"role=\"extension\">.kgm</literal>. It should begin with <sgmltag "
"class=\"starttag\">map</sgmltag> and end with <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">"
"map</sgmltag>."
msgstr ""
"O ficheiro de descrición é preciso e a súa extensión é <literal role=\"extension\">.kgm</literal>. "
"Debera comezar con <sgmltag class=\"starttag\">map</sgmltag> e rematar con <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">map</sgmltag>."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid "Inside of those tags there should be:"
msgstr "Dentro desas marcas debera haber:"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">mapFile</sgmltag> and <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">"
"mapFile</sgmltag>: the name of the file (without any path) containing the map "
"image, &eg; <quote>europe.png</quote>."
msgstr ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">mapFile</sgmltag> e <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">mapFile</sgmltag>: "
"o nome do ficheiro (sen rota) que contén a imaxe do mapa, &eg; <quote>europe.png</quote>."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">name</sgmltag> and <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">"
"name</sgmltag>: the name of map, &eg; <quote>Europe</quote>."
msgstr ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">name</sgmltag> e <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">name</sgmltag>: "
"o nome do mapa, &eg; <quote>Europe</quote>."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <sgmltag class=\"starttag\">division</sgmltag> and <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">"
"division</sgmltag> for each division in the map."
msgstr ""
"Unha <sgmltag class=\"starttag\">division</sgmltag> e <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">division</sgmltag> "
"para cada división do mapa."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each division has these tags:"
msgstr "Cada división ten tres marcas:"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:345
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">name</sgmltag> and <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">"
"name</sgmltag>: the name of the division, &eg; <quote>Albania</quote>."
msgstr ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">name</sgmltag> e <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">name</sgmltag>: "
"o nome da división, &eg; <quote>Albania</quote>."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">capital</sgmltag> and <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">"
"capital</sgmltag>: the name of the capital of the division, &eg; <quote>"
"Tirana</quote>."
msgstr ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">capital</sgmltag> e <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">capital</sgmltag>: "
"o nome da capital da división, &eg; <quote>Tirana</quote>."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">ignore</sgmltag> and <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">"
"ignore</sgmltag>: can be set to <userinput>yes</userinput>, <userinput>"
"allowClickMode</userinput> and <userinput>no</userinput>"
". If this tag is set to <userinput>yes</userinput> then the division will be "
"ignored when asking for divisions in that map. It is then as if this division "
"does not exist in &kgeography; quiz modes. If this tag is set to <userinput>"
"allowClickMode</userinput> then &kgeography; will ask for the division in the "
"<guibutton>Click Division in Map...</guibutton> mode but not in other quiz "
"modes. Setting this tag to <userinput>no</userinput> "
"means the division will appear in all modes (browse and quizzes). This tag is "
"optional and when there is no <sgmltag class=\"starttag\">ignore</sgmltag> "
"tag that means as it is set to <userinput>no</userinput>. For example <quote>"
"Algeria</quote> has this tag set to <userinput>yes</userinput> in the <quote>"
"Europe</quote> map which means that <quote>Algeria</quote> "
"will not be part of any quiz in the <quote>Europe</quote> map."
msgstr ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">ignore</sgmltag> e <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">ignore</sgmltag>: "
"pode ser axustado a <userinput>yes</userinput>, <userinput>allowClickMode</userinput> e "
"<userinput>no</userinput>. Se está como <userinput>yes</userinput> entón a división será "
"ignorada ao perguntar por divisións do mapa. Será como se a división non existise para os xogos "
"de perguntas de &kgeography;. Se está como <userinput>allowClickMode</userinput> entón "
"&kgeography; perguntará pola división no modo <guibutton>Premer División no Mapa...</guibutton> "
"pero en nengún outro modo de perguntas. Se está como <userinput>no</userinput> entón a "
"división aparecerá en todos os modos. Esta marca <sgmltag class=\"starttag\">ignore</sgmltag> "
"é opcional e cando non a hai significará que está axustada ao valor <userinput>no</userinput>. "
"Por exemplo <quote>Arxelia</quote> ten esta marca posta a <userinput>yes</userinput> no mapa "
"<quote>Europa</quote> o que significa que non aparecerá en nengunha pergunta referente ao "
"mapa de <quote>Europa</quote>."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">flag</sgmltag> and <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">"
"flag</sgmltag>: the file (without any path) containing the flag of the "
"division, &eg; <quote>albania.png</quote>. This tag is optional. Not needed for "
"the divisions whose <sgmltag class=\"starttag\">ignore</sgmltag> "
"tag is set to <userinput>yes</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">flag</sgmltag> e <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">flag</sgmltag>: "
"o ficheiro (sen rota) que contén a bandeira da división, &eg; <quote>albania.png</quote>. "
"Esta marca é opcional. Non é precisa para as división que teñan a marca "
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">ignore</sgmltag> posta a <userinput>yes</userinput>."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">color</sgmltag> and <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">"
"color</sgmltag>: the color the division has in the map."
msgstr ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">color</sgmltag> e <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">color</sgmltag>: "
"a cor da división no mapa."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid "The color is defined using three tags:"
msgstr "A cor é definida mediante tres marcas:"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">red</sgmltag> and <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">"
"red</sgmltag>: red component of the color. Valid values are between 0 and 255."
msgstr ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">red</sgmltag> e <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">red</sgmltag>: "
"a componente vermella da cor. Só serven valores entre 0 e 255."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">green</sgmltag> and <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">"
"green</sgmltag>: green component of the color. Valid values are between 0 and "
"255."
msgstr ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">green</sgmltag> e <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">green</sgmltag>: "
"a componente verde da cor. Só serven valores entre 0 e 255."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">blue</sgmltag> and <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">"
"blue</sgmltag>: blue component of the color. Valid values are between 0 and "
"255."
msgstr ""
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">blue</sgmltag> e <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">blue</sgmltag>: "
"a componente azul da cor. Só serven valores entre 0 e 255."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is convenient to create 2 or 3 false divisions like <quote>Water</quote>"
", <quote>Frontier</quote> and <quote>Coast</quote> and set them with the "
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">ignore</sgmltag> tag set to <userinput>"
"yes</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"É conveniente criar 2 ou 3 división falsas como <quote>Auga</quote>, <quote>Fronteira</quote> "
"e <quote>Costa</quote> e porlles a marca <sgmltag class=\"starttag\">ignore</sgmltag> como "
"<userinput>yes</userinput>."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid "All names (capitals and divisions) must be in English."
msgstr "Todos os nomes (de capitais e divisións) deben estar en Inglés."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid "Map file"
msgstr "Ficheiro do Mapa"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The map file is quite simple but laborious to create. It has to be in <acronym>"
"PNG</acronym> format. You can find some maps to transform at <ulink "
"url=\"http://www.odci.gov/cia/publications/factbook/docs/refmaps.html\">"
"Cia Reference Maps</ulink>. If no map fits your needs you can download the "
"<ulink "
"url=\"http://www.odci.gov/cia/publications/factbook/reference_maps/pdf/political"
"_world.pdf\">world pdf</ulink>, take a screenshot of it and work from it. Each "
"division in the map should have one and only one color. To achieve this you can "
"use image processing programs like <application>The Gimp</application> "
"and <application>Kolourpaint</application>."
msgstr ""
"Criar o mapa é sinxelo pero traballoso. Debe estar no formato <acronym>PNG</acronym>. "
"Pode atopar algúns mapas para transformar en <ulink url=\"http://www.odci.gov/cia/publications/factbook/docs/refmaps.html\">"
"Mapas de Referencia Cia</ulink>. Se nengún se axusta ás súas necesidades pode obter o "
"<ulink url=\"http://www.odci.gov/cia/publications/factbook/reference_maps/pdf/political_world.pdf\">"
"world pdf</ulink>, tomar unha captura de pantalla del e traballar desde el. Cada división no mapa "
"debe ter unha única cor. Para acadar isto pode usar programas de procesamento de imaxes como "
"<application>Krita</application> ou <application>Kolourpaint</application>."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid "Flags"
msgstr "Bandeiras"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have used the <sgmltag class=\"starttag\">flag</sgmltag> "
"tag you should provide the flag files. They have to be in <acronym>PNG</acronym> "
"format and better if they are 300x200 pixels and you provide a <acronym>"
"SVG</acronym> file for it. To obtain <acronym>SVG</acronym> "
"flags of almost all countries in the world and some other divisions, you can "
"consult the <ulink "
"url=\"http://www.sodipodi.com/index.php3?section=clipart/flags\">"
"Sodipodi flags collection</ulink>."
msgstr ""
"Se usou a marca <sgmltag class=\"starttag\">flag</sgmltag> deberá fornecer os ficheiros "
"coas bandeiras. Deben estar no formato <acronym>PNG</acronym> e preférese que estexan a "
"300x200 pixel e que forneza un <acronym>SVG</acronym> para elas. Para obter bandeiras "
"<acronym>SVG</acronym> de caseque todos os países do mundo e outras divisións, pode "
"consultar a <ulink url=\"http://www.sodipodi.com/index.php3?section=clipart/flags\">Colección "
"de bandeiras de Sodipodi</ulink>."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:399
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to test"
msgstr "Como probá-lo"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before sending your map to Albert <email>tsdgeos@terra.es</email>"
", you should test it to see it has no errors. To achieve that, you have to do "
"the following: <itemizedlist> <listitem> <para>Put the map description and map "
"image file in <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>"
"/share/apps/kgeography/</filename></para> </listitem> <listitem> <para>"
"Put the flag <acronym>PNG</acronym> files (if any) in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/apps/kgeography/flags/</filenam"
"e></para> </listitem> </itemizedlist> Once that has been done you should be "
"able of opening your map from inside &kgeography;."
msgstr ""
"Antes de enviar o seu mapa para Albert <email>tsdgeos@terra.es</email>, debe "
"probá-lo para verificar que non haxa erros. Para acadar isto, terá que facer o seguinte: "
"<itemizedlist><listitem><para>Pór a descrición do mapa e o ficheiro de imaxe do mapa "
"en <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/apps/kgeography/</filename>"
"</para></listitem>"
"<listitem><para>Pór os ficheiros <acronym>PNG</acronym> das bandeiras (se as hai) en "
"<filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/apps/kgeography/flags/</filename></para>"
"</listitem></itemizedlist> Canto teña feito isto debería poder abrir o seu mapa desde &kgeography;."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you don't know which is your <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>"
"KDEDIR</envar></filename>, type <userinput><command>kde-config</command> "
"<option>--prefix</option></userinput> in a shell."
msgstr ""
"Se non sabe cal é o seu <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>, escreba "
"</filename><userinput><command>kde-config</command> <option>--prefix</option></userinput> "
"nunha shell."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid "Non political maps"
msgstr "Mapas non-políticos"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid "Is it possible to do non-political maps? Yes, it is!"
msgstr "É posíbel confeccionar mapas non-políticos? Si, é-o!"

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:420
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Example of how to create a non political map</screeninfo>"
msgstr "<screeninfo>Exemplo de como criar un mapa non-político</screeninfo>"

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Example of how to create a non political map</phrase>"
msgstr "<phrase>Exemplo de como criar un mapa non-político</phrase>"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Of course, the division concept can be extended to a river or a mountain. "
"During the creation of the map, you should keep in mind that most times the "
"river or mountain will be too small that you should provide an additional "
"clicking area. In this example the river would have the maroon area and color "
"&lt;20,76,34&gt; as its identifier."
msgstr ""
"Por suposto, o conceito de división pode ser ampliado a un río ou montaña. "
"Durante a criación do mapa, debe lembrar que a maioría das veces o río ou montaña será pequeno "
"de mais e que por ende debe ter unha área adicional para premer. Neste exemplo o río ha ter "
"unha área marrón e a cor &lt;20,76,34&gt; como identificador."

